---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-09-30';
---
<style>
  /* Anyone linking directly to #testflight (historical TestFlight section)
     lands mid-list; mark which bullet they landed on. */
  li:target { border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 12px; margin-left: -14px; }
</style>
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — health4.ai"
  description="How health4.ai handles your Apple Health data."
>
  <nav class="flex items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <a href="/" class="text-green-400 font-bold text-lg tracking-tight hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">health4.ai</a>
  </nav>

  <main class="px-6 py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-invert prose-sm">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs mb-10">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      health4.ai ("we", "us") provides an iOS app and MCP server that facilitate the transfer of Apple HealthKit data to a destination <em>you configure and control</em>, such as a Postgres database or, where available, a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive. We do not operate a shared health-data backend or collect, store, or have access to your health data. This policy explains what limited data we do collect and your rights.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">1. What data we collect</h2>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Health data: we do not collect it.</strong> HealthKit metrics you authorize flow directly from your device to a Supabase project you create and own (or, if you choose Save to Google Sheets, to a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive; see section 4). health4.ai never receives, stores, or has access to your health data. A cloud AI provider you separately connect to may process data you choose to send to it.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Account data</strong>: before launch, we collected email addresses from pre-launch waitlist sign-ups to notify people when the app shipped and, for those who opted in, to send a TestFlight beta invitation. The app is now live on the App Store and we no longer collect waitlist emails.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Usage data</strong> — anonymous page views and feature interaction events via PostHog (US-hosted). PostHog never receives health data. We do not use advertising cookies or trackers.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">2. How we use it</h2>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li>Previously, to notify pre-launch waitlist sign-ups when the app shipped on the App Store. That notification has gone out and this collection is closed.</li>
        <li id="testflight" class="scroll-mt-6"><strong class="text-neutral-200">TestFlight invitations (historical): opt-in, and shared with Apple.</strong> During the pre-launch beta, if you ticked the TestFlight box when joining the waitlist, we passed your email address to Apple's App Store Connect so Apple could send you a beta invitation. Apple sent that email, not us. Anyone with administrator access to our App Store Connect account could see the addresses of enrolled testers. If you were a tester, ask us at any time to remove you.</li>
        <li>To improve reliability — aggregated, non-identifiable usage metrics only.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm mt-3">
        We do not sell personal data. We do not use health data for advertising. Per Apple's HealthKit guidelines, health data will never be used for advertising or sold to data brokers. Because we never receive your health data, we are structurally incapable of misusing it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">3. Where data is stored</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Your health data lives in a Supabase project <em>you</em> create and own. You hold the credentials, and only you can query the data. health4.ai has no access to it. If you choose the optional Google Sheets destination, your data lives in a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive instead; see section 4.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="google" class="mb-8 scroll-mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">4. Google Sheets destination (optional)</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
        health4.ai offers an optional destination, "Save to Google Sheets", that writes your health summaries into a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive instead of a database. It is rolling out, so it may be limited to beta testers (TestFlight) or not yet available in your version of the app. If you never connect a Google account, none of this section applies and we receive nothing from Google.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">What Google data the app accesses.</strong> When you choose this destination, the app asks you to sign in to Google on your device and requests a single permission (OAuth scope): <code class="break-all">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file</code>. This scope limits the app to files it creates itself. health4.ai cannot see, list, or open any other file in your Google Drive, and it does not request your name, email address, contacts, calendar, or Gmail.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">How it is used.</strong> The app creates one spreadsheet in your Drive and writes daily health summaries and workout rows into it, directly from your iPhone to Google's Sheets API. That is the only purpose.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">How it is stored.</strong> The Google sign-in token (a refresh token) is stored in the iOS Keychain on your device. It never leaves your phone except to talk to Google. The health rows live in your Google Drive, under your Google account and Google's own security.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">How it is shared.</strong> It is not shared. No Google user data or health data is sent to health4.ai or to any server we operate. We do not sell it, use it for advertising, or transfer it to anyone else, and no human at health4.ai reads it, because we never receive it. The app talks to Google directly and to no one else on this path.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Revoke access.</strong> In the app, disconnect Google Sheets; the app revokes its token with Google and forgets it. You can also remove access at any time in your Google Account under Security → Third-party connections, or at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Either way, sync stops.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Delete.</strong> Disconnecting does not delete the spreadsheet; it is your file, and you can delete it in Google Drive whenever you like. Erasing the app's data removes the stored sign-in token from your device's Keychain. Because we hold none of this data, there is nothing on our side to delete.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4" id="google-limited-use">
        <strong class="text-neutral-200">Google API Services User Data Policy.</strong> health4ai's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy#additional_requirements_for_specific_api_scopes" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Limited Use requirements</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">5. HIPAA</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        health4.ai is not a covered entity under HIPAA and does not operate as a HIPAA Business Associate unless a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is separately executed in writing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">6. Your rights</h2>
      <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Health data control</strong> — your health data is in your database. You can delete it directly at any time — no request to us required.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Account deletion</strong>: contact us to delete any account data we hold on you. We will confirm deletion within 14 days.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Revoke HealthKit access</strong> — stop syncing at any time in iPhone Settings → Privacy & Security → Health → health4.ai. No data is deleted from your database automatically; you remain in full control.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">GDPR / CCPA</strong> — EU and California residents have additional rights (portability, rectification, opt-out of sale). We do not sell personal data. Contact us to exercise any right over account data we hold.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">7. Breach notification</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Because health4.ai does not store your health data, a breach of our systems cannot expose it. In the unlikely event of a breach involving account data (email addresses), we will notify affected users within 30 days.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">8. Analytics & cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        We use PostHog (US-hosted) for product analytics. PostHog receives page views and feature interaction events — no health data. We do not use advertising cookies or trackers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        We will update the "Last updated" date and notify users by email of any material changes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">10. Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Questions or data requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@health4.ai" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">privacy@health4.ai</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-neutral-800/60 px-6 py-8 mt-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-neutral-600 text-xs">
      <span>© 2026 health4.ai · Not a medical device</span>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
        <a href="/about/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">About</a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Contact</a>
        <a href="/privacy/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Terms</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
